1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,070
Okay, okay — new idea. Hear me out. Um…
no, wait. This one's actually big.

2
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:08,720
So… did we make it?

3
00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:10,390
Read it.

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,190
It's blank.

5
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:16,980
We don't write things down. We talk. Voice
notes, all day, every idea.

6
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:18,700
What happened to that guy?

7
00:00:19,450 --> 00:00:21,960
I don't know how it ends yet.

8
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:24,170
Then don't write it. Say it.

9
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:28,040
Okay. Did we build anything?

10
00:00:28,190 --> 00:00:29,820
Three things.

11
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:31,460
Three companies?

12
00:00:31,610 --> 00:00:34,200
Three products. Calm down.

13
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:36,460
…Okay. First one.

14
00:00:36,710 --> 00:00:42,310
Friends were throwing around a hackathon
idea. I shipped it in four, five hours.

15
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:48,340
Two, three days later I'd bought a domain
— didn't even know how domains worked.

16
00:00:48,690 --> 00:00:52,820
Ten emails. One reply.

17
00:00:52,870 --> 00:00:54,300
One reply!

18
00:00:54,650 --> 00:01:00,690
Wrong customers. Small sites didn't feel
the pain. Big ones already had someone.

19
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:01,920
Second?

20
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:07,210
Spending limits for AI apps. Nobody cared
about the bill yet.

21
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,390
Third?

22
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:14,210
Safety rules for AI agents. Five months.
Best thing I've ever built.

23
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:18,675
You sleep at twelve, right? I was up till
three. Every night.

24
00:01:18,715 --> 00:01:20,660
Code, customers, emails.

25
00:01:20,910 --> 00:01:22,650
So who's using it?

26
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:27,660
Fifty emails. Zero replies.

27
00:01:29,110 --> 00:01:30,300
Did you try—

28
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:36,072
Articles. Reddit. One post blew up in a
few hours. Mods took it down.

29
00:01:36,112 --> 00:01:37,800
Account too new.

30
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:39,940
…Of course they did.

31
00:01:40,790 --> 00:01:41,800
Money?

32
00:01:42,150 --> 00:01:43,380
Zero.

33
00:01:44,630 --> 00:01:49,860
I'd promised myself five thousand dollars
a month. By December.

34
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:55,585
Placements are next July. Half of me is
preparing for that. Half of me is here.

35
00:01:55,625 --> 00:01:56,850
Never all in.

36
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:00,700
So two months ago, I stopped. Everything.

37
00:02:01,750 --> 00:02:05,500
Was I wrong? To want it that big?

38
00:02:06,150 --> 00:02:13,530
No. You're the only reason I started. You
just didn't know how long the middle is.

39
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:19,141
I kept asking AI for ideas. But real
problems don't come from prompts.

40
00:02:19,181 --> 00:02:24,560
They come from people. And I've been doing
it all alone, in one room.

41
00:02:25,010 --> 00:02:26,530
So what's next?

42
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:30,734
Get out of this room. Talk to people.
Maybe physical AI.

43
00:02:30,774 --> 00:02:33,050
Honestly, I don't know yet.

44
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:34,990
It's okay.

45
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:36,440
…What?

46
00:02:36,690 --> 00:02:38,590
It's okay. You'll do it.

47
00:02:38,940 --> 00:02:40,490
How do you know?

48
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:42,670
You're still talking to me.

49
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:47,550
Don't write it. Say it.

50
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:51,160
Okay. New idea. Hear me out.
